Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-02-2001||07:21 PM||||It's going in the shop on Friday.  They'll check the fuel pressure among other things.  They should be able to tell me how much of my life savings I'll need to get it right.<P><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierodave||07-03-2001||06:13 AM||||Dave  did you replace or clean the IAC  like I suggested when you got the car?  <P>Remember  I said if the berrymans didn't clear it up in a few tanks that it would need to be removed and cleaned up!(IAC)<P>That car had sat a few months prior to me getting it and the pintle (on the iac) probably has a small amount of corrsion on it.  <BR>I just got an 87 in a few weeks ago that ran exactly the same way!  replaced the IAC cleaned it's bore and no more cold start hesitation!<P>Remove your IAC and take 000 steel wool and clean it up! <P>Spray some trottle body cleaner in the hole where it came from until it runs out clean! (lay a rag under the opening to catch the dirty spray)<P>It just had new plugs and wires put on it!  it does not need a tune-up and the timeing was dead nuts right on. the injectors were just fine in the car. <P>I thought you were going to put the one in from the 85 GT to see if that was the problem?<BR>let me know what you find out <BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Voytek||07-03-2001||05:12 PM||||I was going through something similar until last Friday.  Ok, first, the shop told me that timing was off by 5 degrees (quite significant) and caused a really bad idle.  Done - car now runs smooth when hot.  Second, they told me that one or more injectors can't hold the pressure when the fuel pump kicks in and leak into the cylinders a bit.  That, they tell me, will cause the car to have to be re-started when cold and a bit of a rough idle (again, when cold).  I won't be doing anything about this for a while - it's not that big a deal.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||05:31 PM||||My problem still happens when she's hot, but not nearly as bad.  One of the things the shop's going to check is the fuel pressure.  I'll be sure to print this thread and give it to them so they can get an idea what other Fiero owners have experienced.  They're smart, but they don't work on Fieros every day (well...except for mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
